1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,378
Every skin app gives you a score, then forgets
it.

2
00:00:03,850 --> 00:00:07,978
Skin Ledger keeps the record: dated scans
against your own baseline.

3
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:10,378
Moves under three points are marked flat.

4
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:14,956
Here is one: four weeks, four scans.

5
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:21,396
Not a population average, so lighting can't
pass as progress.

6
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:28,416
Log a change and it shows what followed. Since
azelaic acid, acne is up twenty-three.

7
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:32,688
Sleep and water on the same axis. A pattern is
not a cause.

8
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:41,896
Point the camera at a label. The ingredients
are parsed in two seconds, and a model repairs
what OCR mangles.

9
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:46,156
Ask why acne improved. It answers from your
numbers, never the photo.

10
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:53,360
Four calls: register, upload, analyse, poll.
The masks come back with the result.

11
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:56,540
The product isn't the score. It's the record.
